---
layout: layouts/piece.njk
title: "The Café — Macho Nachos Post (1080 × 1350)"
canvasW: "1080px"
canvasH: "1350px"
pageCss: "/assets/css/studio/fb-macho-nachos.css"

# The day. The plate, its price and its toppings come from that day in
# specials.json; the cream puffs' price and kinds from desserts.json
# (npm run desserts). The caption (fb-macho-nachos.11tydata.js) reads the
# same, so the picture and the words can't disagree.
postDate: "2026-11-03"
dessert: "Cream Puffs"
# Mitch's photos from 2026-11-03, cropped to the cards' shape and stripped
# of camera data (originals in photos-originals/): the nachos to go, and a
# cream puff and a chocolate one side by side. Without a file, that card
# shows its words only.
nachosPhoto: "/assets/studio/macho-nachos.jpg"
puffsPhoto: "/assets/studio/cream-puffs.jpg"

tags: studio
studioWeekly: true
studioData: ["specials.json", "desserts.json"]
studioTitle: "Macho Nachos and cream puffs — Facebook post"
studioCategory: "Social"
studioSize: "1080 × 1350 px · portrait feed post"
studioNote: "A rainy-day post for one day's lunch special, Macho Nachos, with the cream puffs for dessert. The plate, price and toppings come from that day in specials.json, the cream puffs from desserts.json: a kind Square counts at 0 is left off, so run npm run desserts after counting them. The photos are src/assets/studio/macho-nachos.jpg and cream-puffs.jpg (plain left, chocolate right); without one, that card shows its words only."
studioW: 1080
studioH: 1350
studioOrder: 25
---
{#- One day's plate and a dessert, a row each, photo beside the words.
    The rainy-day line ("Don't let the rain prevent you from having a Macho
    day") is the caption's opening only: the picture is just the plate and
    the dessert (client 2026-11-03).

    THE PLATE is the day in specials.json, found by postDate: its name, its
    price (the day's own or the usual one), the drink, and its leaveOff
    list, which is what comes on it. The nacho cheese note is in the
    caption, where there's room to say it properly.

    THE CREAM PUFFS are desserts.json's: the price, and the kinds Square
    still counts (puffKinds, worked out in the .11tydata.js). Count them on
    the kitchen board and run npm run desserts before building this.

    Every size is set for the ~540px a portrait post shows at on a phone:
    nothing a customer needs is under 24px. -#}
{%- set o = site.opening %}
<div class="canvas mn">

    <header class="mn-head">
        <div class="wordmark wordmark--light wordmark--hero mn-wordmark">
            {% inlineSvg "/assets/thecafe.svg", "", site.name %}
        </div>
        <p class="p-label mn-range">{{ postDate | dayDate("long") }} &middot; {{ site.address.locality }}, {{ site.address.region }}</p>
    </header>

    <div class="mn-body">
        <section class="mn-card">
            {%- if nachosPhoto | hasAsset %}
            <img class="mn-photo" src="{{ nachosPhoto }}" alt="">
            {%- endif %}
            <div class="mn-words">
                <p class="p-label mn-label">Lunch special</p>
                <h2 class="p-display mn-name">{{ day.special }}</h2>
                <p class="p-display-italic mn-price">{{ plate.price }}{% if specials.includesDrink %} with a drink{% endif %}</p>
                {%- if plate.toppings %}
                <p class="p-body mn-detail">{{ plate.toppings }}</p>
                {%- endif %}
                <p class="p-label mn-served">From 11am</p>
            </div>
        </section>

        {#- The photo on the other side, so the two rows zig-zag. #}
        <section class="mn-card mn-card--flip">
            {%- if puffsPhoto | hasAsset %}
            <img class="mn-photo" src="{{ puffsPhoto }}" alt="">
            {%- endif %}
            <div class="mn-words">
                <p class="p-label mn-label">For dessert</p>
                <h2 class="p-display mn-name">{{ dessert }}</h2>
                <p class="p-display-italic mn-price">{{ puffs.price }} each</p>
                <p class="p-body mn-detail">{{ puffs.kinds | capitalize }}, while they last</p>
            </div>
        </section>
    </div>

    <footer class="mn-foot">
        <p class="p-display mn-foot-call">{{ site.phone }} <span class="dot">&middot;</span> {{ site.social.website }}</p>
        <p class="p-body mn-foot-line">{{ postDate | dayDate("weekday") }} {{ o.opens.time | replace(":00", "") }}{{ o.opens.meridiem }} &ndash; {{ o.closes.time | replace(":00", "") }}{{ o.closes.meridiem }} &middot; {{ site.address.street }}, {{ site.address.locality }}, {{ site.address.region }}</p>
    </footer>

</div>
